# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — wiki home

This is the landing page for the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** wiki. The content here lives at `llm-wiki/wiki/` inside the project root.

## Start here

- **What lives where**: see [_MAP.md](./_MAP.md) (always-loaded into context) or [_INDEX.md](./_INDEX.md) (full scannable list)
- **Project scope**: see [README.md](./README.md)
- **How to use it**: see `../how-to/getting-started.md`

## Quick reference

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `/wiki-search "<query>"` | Look something up |
| `/wiki-update <url>` | Add an external reference |
| `/wiki-cycle` | Full ingest pipeline (research) |
| `/wrap-up` | End-of-session distillation (development) |
| `/wiki-promote --review` | Approve staged entries from `_inbox/proposed/` |

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or `_INDEX.md` — they're auto-generated
- Don't promote directly to `wiki/<folder>/` — always stage via `_inbox/proposed/`
- Don't suppress contradictions — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked

## Concept gaps

When you notice a project, person, framework, or paper that should be tracked but doesn't have an entry yet, add it to [`concept-gaps-things-mentioned-not-yet-covered.md`](./concept-gaps-things-mentioned-not-yet-covered.md) so the next `/wiki-cycle --discover` pass can pick it up.

(That file doesn't exist yet — create it the first time you have a gap to track. Format: one row per gap with the term, where it was mentioned, and a priority.)
